direction: down

vars: {
  d2-config: {
    theme-id: 0
    layout-engine: dagre
    pad: 40
  }
}

classes: {
  ext:   {style.fill: "#eceff1"; style.stroke: "#90a4ae"}
  go:    {style.fill: "#e3f2fd"; style.stroke: "#1976d2"}
  py:    {style.fill: "#ede7f6"; style.stroke: "#5e35b1"}
  lib:   {style.fill: "#e0f2f1"; style.stroke: "#00897b"}
  store: {style.fill: "#e8f5e9"; style.stroke: "#2e7d32"}
  mem:   {style.fill: "#fff8e1"; style.stroke: "#f9a825"}
  ctl:   {style.fill: "#e5e7eb"; style.stroke: "#37474f"}
  bad:   {style.fill: "#ffebee"; style.stroke: "#c62828"}
}

title: "What is actually PROVEN, and what has never been touched.\nObserved on integration/wave1, 2026-10-02. Every count below came from a command run at the repo root, not from a doc." {
  style.bold: true
  style.font-size: 21
}

# ================================================================ BAND 1 ====
# Automatically verified. These are cheap precisely because none of them
# touches a socket, a credential or the checkpoint — which is also exactly
# why they cannot speak for a live run.

auto: "1 · VERIFIED AUTOMATICALLY — the gates, and what each one really checks" {
  class: ctl

  lint: "make lint  →  `lint: vet`, then a gofmt sweep over MODULES\n`go vet ./...` then `gofmt -l .` in each of the four modules:\ncore · services/ingestion · services/execution · services/jobs\nThe root is not a Go module — go.work stitches them, so every target in\nthis Makefile loops per module and exits 1 on the first failure.\nOBSERVED: 4 vet passes silent, 0 gofmt diffs, `lint ok`.\nWhat it does NOT cover: a single line of Python. There is no linter for\nservices/inference at all, so a 325-line FastAPI module is ungated." {
    class: go
  }

  test: "make test  →  `go test -race ./...` in all four modules\nOBSERVED: 12 packages with tests, every one ok. 298 top-level test\nfunctions plus 214 subtests = 512 cases. 512 PASS, 0 FAIL, 0 SKIP, and\nnot one 'DATA RACE' line in the output.\nBy module — core 155 functions, services/jobs 70, services/execution 47,\nservices/ingestion 26.\n6 of the 18 packages have no test files and so contribute nothing:\ncore, core/contracts, core/testutil and the three cmd/server packages." {
    class: go
  }

  race: "Why `-race`, quoted from the Makefile itself (lines 28-30)\n\"Ingestion's exactly-once bar completion and the risk engine's\nidempotency claim are only meaningful if they hold under concurrency,\nand a plain `go test` will not notice a data race.\"\nTwo properties on this page are concurrency claims, and only -race can see\neither: `TestRolloverWritesCandleExactlyOnce` (pipeline_test.go) and the\n`IDEM:` claim that lives inside one `e.mu.Lock()` critical section — see\n23-crosscut-idempotency. Both are silently unfalsifiable without it." {
    class: go
  }

  testpy: "make test-python  →  a RESTRICTED file list, and the restriction IS the point\nPYTEST_PERMITTED := model/tests/test_base.py model/tests/test_heuristic_model.py\n`pytest app/tests` plus those two files — nothing else is on the line.\nOBSERVED: 283 passed = 237 in app/tests + 46 in the two permitted files.\nThe 23 tests in model/tests/test_tabfm_model.py are deliberately NOT in that\nlist. This is the mechanism that stops the default gate from ever reaching\nthe ~6.6GB checkpoint on a 14GB box with the OOM killer live. `make\ntabfm-weights` and every HuggingFace download are off-limits for the same\nreason. See band 3 for why that file list is also broken." {
    class: py
  }

  bt: "make backtest  →  the walk-forward harness, and the one assertion inside it\nThe assertion that makes any number from this harness worth reading is\n`test_no_lookahead_scores_and_candidates_are_identical` in\napp/tests/test_backtest.py: `corrupt_tail` rewrites the final bar into a 6x\njump and asserts that EVERY score, candidate set, entry price and idempotency\nkey is unchanged. A backtest that leaks the future is worse than no backtest,\nbecause a leaking one is indistinguishable from a real edge.\nAlso pinned there: incremental mode is numerically identical to rebuild, at\nO(n) per symbol. OBSERVED: runs to completion, exit 0." {
    class: py
  }

  diag: "make diagrams-check  →  the parse gate for this directory\nD2 v0.9.0 has no --quiet and no --dry-run, so the CI form genuinely compiles\nevery .d2 to a throwaway SVG inside `mktemp -d` and deletes it. It proves the\nfile parses and every shape reference resolves.\nIt proves NOTHING about whether the shapes are true. A diagram that lies\nabout the system parses exactly as cleanly as one that does not — which is\nwhy this page cites a command and a file for every claim it makes.\nOBSERVED on this branch: failed 0 across the set." {
    class: ctl
  }

  ledger: "THE ACTUAL LEDGER — counted, not estimated\nGo      12 packages · 298 test functions · 512 cases · 512 PASS · 0 FAIL · 0 SKIP · 0 races\nPython  283 passed (237 app/tests + 46 permitted) · 23 tests never collected\nBacktest  2000 bars x 3 symbols · 5637 scored · 627 trades · exit 0\nDiagrams  every .d2 in docs/diagrams parses\nNot one of these needed a Kite credential, an open socket, or 7 GiB of free\nmemory. That is exactly why they are cheap enough to run on every save — and\nexactly why they are silent about everything in bands 2 and 3.\nEvery one of these counts was produced by a person typing one of these five\ncommands, by hand, at a moment in time. Nothing runs them automatically —\nsee the NO CI node in band 3." {
    class: ctl
    style.bold: true
  }

  ceiling: "The honest ceiling on band 1\nThese five commands are a FLOOR, not a certificate. A green run means the\nshape of the code is sound; it says nothing about whether the code has ever\nmet the thing it exists to trade against. Read this page as: 'these properties\nare checked', never as 'these properties hold'." {
    class: ctl
  }

  test -> race: "and this is the reason why"
  lint -> ledger: "4 vet passes,\n0 findings"
  test -> ledger: "12 packages,\n512 PASS"
  testpy -> ledger: "283 passed"
  bt -> ledger: "627 trades,\nexit 0"
  diag -> ledger: "failed 0"
  ledger -> ceiling: "the floor,\nnot a certificate"
}

# ================================================================ BAND 2 ====
# Manual, human, and genuinely useful — provided you know what it cannot see.

human: "2 · VERIFIED MANUALLY — a human starts it, a human reads it" {
  class: ctl

  dev: "make dev  →  four seconds of `sleep 4`, then four processes\nmake build, then `make stop`, then ingestion on :9090, execution on\n:8080 + :9091, jobs on :9092 and — only if the venv exists — inference on\n:8000. Each gets `MFT_CONFIG=configs/config.yaml` and its own\nMFT_METRICS_ADDR, because they all read one config file and cannot share a\nport. Logs land in .dev/*.log.\nThe decisive fact: it starts with NO credentials at all. That is what makes\nit runnable, and also what bounds what it can prove." {
    class: ctl
  }

  h_ex: "curl :8080/v1/health  →  503 + status \"degraded\" is the CORRECT ANSWER\nhandleHealth calls `a.health.Readyz(ctx)`, which runs `probeBroker`, which\ncalls `orders.GetPositions(ctx)` — the cheapest authenticated read Kite\noffers, and the one that fails first on a missing or expired token.\nconfigs/config.yaml ships `access_token: \"\"`, so the probe fails,\n`Report.Status = StatusDegraded` (core/metrics/health.go:97) and the handler\nanswers 503 rather than 200. http.go:358: \"a process that cannot reach Kite\nis not trading, however healthy it looks.\"\nA green 200 here would have been the bug." {
    class: go
  }

  h_inf: "curl :8000/healthz  →  `runtime.predictor.is_loaded()`, and the same story\nconfigs/config.yaml says `inference.model: tabfm`, so build_runtime asks\n`Predictor.from_name(\"tabfm\")`. `_load` then hits its OWN free-memory\npreflight — WEIGHTS_FOOTPRINT_BYTES 7 GiB + WEIGHTS_HEADROOM_BYTES 1 GiB = 8\nGiB required, and this machine reports about 4 — and raises\n`ModelUnavailableError` instead of letting the kernel do it.\nSo: model_loaded false, and POST /v1/predict answers 503 MODEL_NOT_LOADED.\nRefusing in typed code is the feature, not the failure." {
    class: py
  }

  proves: "WHAT A RUNNING SYSTEM PROVES — and it is not nothing\nFour processes bind their ports. configs/config.yaml parses. The metrics\nregistries register without a duplicate-collector panic. The DuckDB\nconnection, the fluxKV cache, the feature builder and the risk chain all\nconstruct. Every dependency check reports its true state instead of a\nconvenient one.\nThat is a real claim about wiring, and it is the only end-to-end evidence\nthis repository currently has." {
    class: ctl
  }

  notproves: "WHAT IT DOES NOT PROVE — no tick, no candle, no order.\nNot one instrument has ever streamed. data/candles/ is empty, which is why\n`make backtest` has to default to `--synthetic`. Nothing has crossed the\nKite boundary in either direction. No metric has ever been incremented by a\nreal broker response, because no real broker response has ever existed:\nmft_execution_orders_placed_total and its rejection siblings are declared\nand unit-tested against fakes, and that is the entire extent of their history.\nDisclosure for this page: `make status` on this checkout at the time of\nwriting reported all five ports down. Nothing was left running, and no\nservice was started to produce the claims above — they are read from the\nhandlers, their config and their tests, not from a live curl." {
    class: ctl
  }

  dev -> h_ex: "start it, then ask"
  dev -> h_inf: "start it, then ask"
  h_ex -> proves: "a refusal that is\nthe system working"
  h_inf -> proves: "same shape, Python side"
  proves -> notproves: "and still:"
}

# ================================================================ BAND 3 ====
# The band this page exists for. Deliberately the loudest thing on the sheet.

unverified: "3 · NOT VERIFIED — the gaps, stated plainly" {
  class: bad
  style.stroke-dash: 8
  style.stroke-width: 3
  style.fill: "#ffebee"

  nolive: "NO LIVE PATH HAS EVER RUN.\nThere are no Kite credentials — `access_token: \"\"` in configs/config.yaml\nand no `.env` anywhere on this machine. The WebSocket streamer, the\nminute-close fold and the feature pipeline have therefore only ever been\ndriven by fakes and `httptest` servers: 7 Go test files use httptest, and\nservices/jobs/fakekite_test.go is a hand-written Kite stand-in.\nAn httptest server can be told to drop a connection between two frames. It\ncannot drop one mid-frame, cannot send the ~30s ping control frame, cannot\nreorder, and cannot go quiet for exactly 90s. So the reconnect path has been\nproven against A disconnect; it has never been proven against the fault Kite\nactually produces." {
    class: bad
    style.stroke-dash: 4
  }

  weights: "THE TABFM WEIGHTS HAVE NEVER BEEN LOADED. DELIBERATELY.\n`TabFMModel` is written and unit-tested against a FAKE checkpoint; all 23\ntests in model/tests/test_tabfm_model.py never read the real one. The cached\nweights sit on disk at ~/.cache/huggingface/hub/models--google--tabfm-1.0.0-pytorch\nand are off limits — unread, uncopied, unloaded.\nPlan.md §0 records the trade verbatim: \"we accept that CI cannot prove the\nweights load, in exchange for CI never risking the OOM killer.\"\nVerifying real inference is a MANUAL step — a human, every other service\nstopped, with the memory free. It is not a test and must never become one.\nThe one guard that IS automated is the free-memory preflight in _load:\n7 GiB footprint + 1 GiB headroom, and this machine reports about 4, so\n`make dev` gets a typed ModelUnavailableError and `model_loaded: false`\nrather than the kernel's SIGKILL.\nTHE CONSEQUENCE, stated once: no artefact anywhere in this repo has ever been\nproduced by a real TabFM forward pass." {
    class: bad
    style.stroke-dash: 4
  }

  golden: "THE GOLDEN FEATURE VECTORS EXIST IN TWO FILES, AND NOTHING COMPARES THEM.\nGo:  core/features/golden_test.go\nPy:  services/inference/app/tests/fixtures/feature_golden.json\nSame 64 bars, same 7 expected feature rows, both asserted at 1e-9 relative.\nThe Python fixture is \"transcribed from\" the Go file — a human copy, not a\nshared artefact. The test module's own docstring says it: \"if the Go builder\nchanges and this file is not updated, both suites still pass and the two have\ndrifted.\"\nBoth suites are green right now, which is exactly equally consistent with the\ntwo implementations agreeing and with the 18-column contract having quietly\nforked. One commit — generate the JSON from the Go builder, or embed one file\nboth sides read — closes it. It is not done." {
    class: bad
    style.stroke-dash: 4
  }

  fill202: "202 Accepted / FILLED IS UNREACHABLE END TO END.\n`outcomeFor(contracts.OrderTypeMarket)` returns 202 / FILLED. It is\nimplemented, specified in docs/contracts.md §7, and unit-tested by\n`TestOutcomeFor`. No request can reach it, because the risk chain sizes a\nposition as quantity * price — risk/book.go:116 `notional := float64(sig.Quantity)\n* sig.Price` and risk/checks.go:32 — and `validateOrder` refuses `price <= 0`.\nA market order has no price. http.go:414 calls this \"a gap and not a design\".\nSo this service places LIMIT orders only, and ExecuteSignal returns an order\nid with no fill state at all (http.go:410): the transport cannot observe a\nfill even in principle. `FILLED` is a well-specified value for a code path\nnobody has ever taken." {
    class: bad
    style.stroke-dash: 4
  }

  noci: "NO CI IS CONFIGURED. NOTHING HERE RUNS UNLESS A HUMAN TYPES IT.\nChecked and absent: .github/, .gitlab-ci.yml, .travis.yml, .circleci/,\nJenkinsfile, .buildkite/, .woodpecker/. There is no workflow, no hook, no\nschedule, no pre-push. `make lint`, `make test`, `make test-python`,\n`make backtest` and `make diagrams-check` are five local commands that a\nperson remembers to run.\nEvery number on this page was produced by a person running one of them by\nhand, at a moment in time, on one machine, with nothing recording that it\nhappened. Plan.md §6 calls these the gates. They are not gates until\nsomething invokes them, and nothing does." {
    class: bad
    style.stroke-dash: 4
  }

  synth: "`make backtest` DEFAULTS TO SYNTHETIC DATA. IT PROVES PLUMBING AND NOTHING ELSE.\nDefault ARGS = `--synthetic --bars 2000 --feature-mode incremental`, because\ndata/candles/ is empty. app/synth.py is geometric Brownian motion with\ndrift(annual) = 0.000 — a random walk.\nThe recorded run: 5637 bars scored, 627 trades, 0 wins / 627 loss, net -3.73%\non Rs 1,000,000, Sharpe per bar -1.526. ZERO OUT OF 627 IS THE CORRECT\nOUTCOME, not a bug — forecasting a random number generator whose parameters\nthe harness itself chose.\nThe cost is what makes the ledger total: gross P&L +Rs 187.30 over 627 trades\n(mean +Rs 0.30, sigma Rs 13.25) against Rs 59.71 of charges per trade, i.e.\n4.5 sigma. 321 of the 627 trades were gross-POSITIVE; the strategy just\ncannot pay the bill. The harness printed \"THIS IS NOT A STRATEGY RESULT\"\nbefore printing any of it." {
    class: bad
    style.stroke-dash: 4
  }

  mftpy: "AND `make test-python` DOES NOT RUN AS WRITTEN.\nMakefile:44 does `cd ROOT/services/inference` and then invokes the variable\nPY, whose value is the RELATIVE path `services/inference/.venv/bin/python`.\nAfter the cd there is no such file. OBSERVED: `/bin/sh: line 1:\nservices/inference/.venv/bin/python: No such file or directory`, Error 127.\nThe `test -x` guard on PY does not catch it, because from the repo root the\nsymlink `services/inference/.venv` does resolve — which is exactly why the\nfailure is a raw 127 rather than the intended \"run 'make setup' first\".\nRun by hand with an absolute interpreter path it is green: 283 passed. So the\n283 in band 1 came from a manual invocation, not from `make test-python`, and\nthat count is not something the Makefile produced.\n`make backtest` escapes the same trap because Makefile:153 spells its path\nROOT/VENV/bin/python. The Makefile is frozen under AGENTS.md, so this\nis a report and not a patch." {
    class: bad
    style.stroke-dash: 4
  }

  weights -> synth: "the backtest never even asked TabFM;\nit ran heuristic-v1"
  nolive -> fill202: "and so 202 has never\nbeen observed live"
  nolive -> golden: "the same silence, inside the repo\nrather than outside it"
}

auto -> human: "what -race cannot check,\na human starting the stack can"
human -> unverified: "and what a human running it cannot check either"
unverified -> footer: "every claim in all three bands is checkable at these paths,\nand every count is reproducible by re-running the five commands"

footer: "Derived from — and every number above is reproducible by re-running these, from the repo root, on integration/wave1:\n`make lint` · `make test` · `make status` · `make backtest` · `make diagrams-check`, plus one hand-typed pytest with an absolute interpreter path (see band 3)\nMakefile — MODULES, PYTEST_PERMITTED, test, test-python, backtest, diagrams-check, dev, status, and the -race comment at lines 28-30\ncore/metrics/health.go (StatusOK, StatusDegraded, Report, Checks, Health.Readyz) · core/metrics/metrics.go (Handler)\nservices/execution/http.go (handleHealth, probeBroker, validateSignal, validateOrder, orderTypeFor, outcomeFor, classify)\nservices/execution/risk/book.go:116 · services/execution/risk/checks.go:32 — the quantity * price sizing that makes a market order unmeasurable\ncore/features/golden_test.go · services/inference/app/tests/test_features_golden.py · services/inference/app/features.py · services/inference/app/tests/support.py (GOLDEN_PATH)\nservices/inference/model/tabfm_model.py (WEIGHTS_FILE, WEIGHTS_FOOTPRINT_BYTES, WEIGHTS_HEADROOM_BYTES, weights_available, _load preflight) · services/inference/model/base.py (InferenceModel)\nservices/inference/app/tests/test_backtest.py (corrupt_tail, test_no_lookahead_scores_and_candidates_are_identical, test_no_lookahead_is_exact_for_every_horizon)\nservices/inference/app/synth.py · services/inference/app/backtest.py · services/inference/app/runtime.py (build_runtime) · services/inference/app/predictor.py (Predictor.from_name)\nservices/ingestion/pipeline_test.go (TestRolloverWritesCandleExactlyOnce, TestBoundaryTickLandsInTheRightBar, TestSweepClosesAQuietBar) · services/jobs/fakekite_test.go\nconfigs/config.yaml · configs/config.example.yaml · core/config/config.go · docs/contracts.md §4 §7 · AGENTS.md · Plan.md §0 §4 §5 §6 · docs/diagrams/STYLE.md" {
  class: ctl
  style.fill: "#ffffff"
  style.stroke-dash: 4
}
